00:05:08,571 --> 00:05:14,571
Welcome to the world of your dreams!

2
00:10:17,142 --> 00:10:23,142
Absolute Beginners is a drama, music, romance film directed by Julien Temple.

3
00:15:25,714 --> 00:15:31,714
A musical adaptation of Colin MacInnes' novel about life in late 1950s London.

4
00:20:34,285 --> 00:20:40,285
Nineteen-year-old photographer Colin is hopelessly in love with model Crepe Suzette, but her
relationships are strictly connected with her progress in the fashion world.

5
00:25:42,857 --> 00:25:48,857
So Colin gets involved with a pop promoter and tries to crack the big time.

6
00:30:51,428 --> 00:30:57,428
Meanwhile, racial tension is brewing in Colin's Notting Hill housing estate...

7
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Colin, Photographer / Narrator, played by Eddie O'Connell.

8
00:41:08,571 --> 00:41:14,571
Suzette, played by Patsy Kensit.

9
00:46:17,142 --> 00:46:23,142
Henley of Mayfair, Dressmaker to the Queen, played by James Fox.

10
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
Vendice Partners, played by David Bowie.

11
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
Arthur, Colin's Dad, played by Ray Davies.

12
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:48,857
Flora, Colin's Mum, played by Mandy Rice-Davies.

13
01:06:51,428 --> 01:06:57,428
Absolute Beginners is a 1986 British musical film adapted from Colin MacInnes'
book about life in late 1950s London, directed by Julien Temple.

14
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The film stars Eddie O' Connell, Patsy Kensit, James Fox, Edward Tudor-Pole, Anita Morris, and
David Bowie, with featured appearances by Sade Adu, Ray Davies, and Steven Berkoff.

15
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
It was screened out of competition at the 1986 Cannes Film Festival.

16
01:22:17,142 --> 01:22:23,142
It received coverage in the British media but was panned by critics and became a box
office failure, although modern reviews have been more favourable.

17
01:27:25,714 --> 01:27:31,714
Bowie's theme song was very popular in the UK, spending nine
weeks on the charts and peaking at number two.

18
01:32:34,285 --> 01:32:40,285
The commercial failure of Absolute Beginners and two other films is blamed for the collapse of
British film studio Goldcrest Films and for Virgin Films withdrawing from production.

19
01:37:42,857 --> 01:37:48,857
The film explores themes of london, england,
photographer, musical, modeling, 1950s.

20
01:42:51,428 --> 01:42:57,428
The tone is emotional.
